---
// what's next: the road from hand-written kernels to tinygrad. safe to edit: the headline, the three .item boxes, and the qr caption.
// the qr code points at the blackhole-py repo (src/qr-repo.ts holds it, made with python qrcode; regenerate it for another link).
import { QR_PATH, QR_SIZE } from '../qr-repo';
import f from '../facts.json';
---
<header>
  <div class="section">what’s next</div>
  <h2>next: no more hand-written kernels</h2>
</header>
<div class="next">
  <div class="items">
    <div class="item"><i>1</i><div><b>a kernel language</b><span>fast blackhole kernels in a few lines: all five cpus and both engines from one program</span></div></div>
    <div class="item"><i>2</i><div><b>a simple compiler</b><span>turns a model’s graph into those kernels: fuses ops, keeps all {f.card.cores} cores busy</span></div></div>
    <div class="item"><i>3</i><div><b>tinygrad on the card</b><span>researchers write <code>model(x)</code> and it just runs, no kernels by hand</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="qr">
    <svg viewBox={`-4 -4 ${QR_SIZE + 8} ${QR_SIZE + 8}`} width="300" height="300" shape-rendering="crispEdges">
      <rect class="qr-bg" x="-4" y="-4" width={QR_SIZE + 8} height={QR_SIZE + 8} />
      <path class="qr-dots" d={QR_PATH} />
    </svg>
    <p>the code behind the demo<br /><code>{f.repo}</code></p>
  </div>
</div>
<style>
  .next { display: flex; gap: 80px; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
  .items { width: 860px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; }
  .item { display: flex; gap: 22px; align-items: center; background: var(--panel); border-left: 6px solid var(--good); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 24px; }
  .item i { font-style: normal; font-size: 48px; font-weight: 800; color: var(--good); width: 36px; flex: none; text-align: center; }
  .item b { display: block; font-size: 34px; }
  .item span { display: block; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.3; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 4px; }
  .qr { text-align: center; width: 420px; }
  .qr svg { border-radius: 10px; }
  /* scanners want dark dots on a light square, in either theme */
  .qr-bg { fill: var(--fg); }
  .qr-dots { fill: var(--bg); }
  :global(:root[data-theme=light]) .qr-bg { fill: var(--bg); }
  :global(:root[data-theme=light]) .qr-dots { fill: var(--fg); }
  .qr p { font-size: 22px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 12px; }
  .qr code { font-size: 17px; white-space: nowrap; }
</style>
